  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Showery and stormy pattern continues through\nSunday. \n\nScattered showers and thunderstorms have erupted this afternoon\nin response to several modes of forcing for ascent. A band of \nmid level vorticity was located from Maryland to southern OH to \nMO, ending with a significant short wave also located near MO. \nThis wave is progged to move east and deepen the overall short \nwave trough tonight through Sunday as it does so. At the \nsurface, a cold front was located from coastal VA and snaked \nthrough our forecast area in VA before stretching towards the \nArkLaTex. \n\nThe front was interacting with moderately unstable air with \ntemperatures ranging from the upper 70s and low 80s in the\nmountains to the mid 80s to 90s in the Piedmont. As of 2 pm, \nSouth Boston had warmed to 96 degrees, with Danville at 94. Dew \npoints were generally in the 60s with a few locations around 70.\nWith the approaching short wave, the front will continue to \nshift slowly south and trigger widespread convection this \nafternoon. For tomorrow, the front will move back northeast as a\nwarm front, bringing moderate rain to the entire area before it\nexits to the east after midnight Saturday night. We are \nexpecting only general thunder for severe weather per SPC both \nthis afternoon/evening and again tomorrow. However, isolated \ndamaging wind gusts will be possible with the strongest storms. \nIn addition, urban, small stream, and isolated flash flooding \nmay be possible as convection trains along the front and with \nrepeated rounds expected. \n\nA few showers/storms may develop Sunday afternoon as another\ncold front moves through, but not expecting anything strong or\norganized. This would mainly impact the Blue Ridge eastward. \nBehind this front, much drier and cooler air arrives for the \nbeginning of next week, perhaps lasting through Wednesday as a \nlarge upper ridge builds in. By Thursday, we will see a similar \nset up to the current event, with a slow-moving, strung out \nfront to our north bringing several chances for rain and storms \nfor the end of the week into next weekend.",
